  "id": "battery-dc-jack-power-v1",
  "name": "9 V power · DC jack and battery, switched by the input jack",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 0
  },
  "description": "How a pedal takes a 9 V supply or a battery, the battery switched off by the input jack. The DC jack (centre negative) puts the supply on V+, through a reverse-polarity diode and the 9 V input filter to V+F (the filter's values from the ProCo Rat, ElectroSmash; the 1N5817 as on Aion FX's boards). The battery's + goes to the DC jack's battery lug, which touches the sleeve only with no plug in, so a supply cuts the battery off; its − goes to the TRS input jack's ring (J1), so the battery is on only while a TS guitar cable is in. Wire J1's T (the in port) to IN's middle. Knobs: Power picks the DC jack or the battery, Input cable pulls the cable.",
  "tags": [
    "power",
    "battery",
    "dc",
    "jack",
    "filter"
  ],
  "template": true,
