      ],
      "note": "Reverse-polarity protection: a Schottky diode in series, as on Aion FX's boards (the Comet's D1, with the same 47 Ω, 100 µF and 100 nF after it). A supply plugged in the wrong way round is blocked; it drops about 0.2 V, so V+F sits a little under 9 V.",
      "type": "diode",
      "model": "1N5817"
    },
    {
      "ref": "J1",
      "pos": [
        -200,
        -140
      ],
      "note": "A TRS input jack switching the battery: its − goes to the ring, and a TS guitar plug's long sleeve joins the ring to ground, so the pedal is on only with a cable in. A TRS cable doesn't switch it on (its ring is its own). Wire T (the in port) to IN's middle, so pulling the cable takes the guitar out too. Knobs: Input cable.",
      "type": "jack",
      "trs": true,
      "label": "Input"
    }
